  "body": "Stacked on #715 (grblHAL post): this branch is #715's head plus one commit, and extends the same registry and test lists. Fork synced at v0.16.0 (through #715's base).\n\n## What changed\n\nA new built-in post, **TinyG** (`assets/posts/tinyg.cps`, 3-axis mill), for Synthetos TinyG controllers, and a generic machine, **TinyG 3-axis** (`assets/machines/tinyg-3axis.mch`). The post is specced from TinyG's public wiki (Gcode Support, Homing and Limits, Flow Control and Footers, Inch and Millimeter Units Mode) and the LinuxCNC G-code reference TinyG states it follows (behaviour only; the firmware source is GPL and was not read), structured after `grblhal.cps`. Decisions in `docs/decisions/836-tinyg-post.md`.\n\n- Header `G21|G20 G17 G90 G91.1 G94 G64`: the words M30 does not reset on TinyG (units, arc-centre mode and path-control mode persist). No `%`, O word, N numbers, G40 or G80; no tool length word (as #710 decided for grblHAL: the measured length belongs to the operator or sender).\n- **No canned cycles**: a CYCLE record writes nothing and the hole's expanded chain posts as plain moves, with the dwell as `G4 P<seconds>` after the move that reaches the bottom; a dwell whose chain never reaches it is refused, not dropped. Tapping is refused by name.\n- **Tool change**: the Z lift, then `T<n> M6` alone on its line, then `M0` on the next - TinyG's M6 only records the tool, so the stop is the operator's change; the first tool gets it too. Tools T1-T31; a larger number is refused by name. Because of that M0 the after-operation stops are pinned in `tinyg_post.rs` rather than through `after_op.rs`'s mill list (whose tests count every M0 as the operator's stop); the home refusal is in that list.\n- **Z lift as grblHAL's** (#715): `G53 G0 Z<safe_retract>` only when the machine file states it, else `G0 Z<clearance>` in the work offset, refused by name when unknown or not above the stock. No G28/G30. The generic machine states no `safe_retract`.\n- **Comments** drop `!` (feed hold), `~` (cycle start), `%` (queue flush), `/`, `{`, `$` and the comment delimiters; a note opening with `msg` is led by \"- \" so TinyG does not echo it as a message. Lines are kept to 191 content bytes (248 usable receive bytes, 192-byte RTS window) and a longer one is refused by name.\n- Lengths at four decimals in either unit (TinyG checks an arc's start and end radius against its centre). Extension `.gcode`.\n- Refused by name: control/wear compensation (G41/G42 are rejected by the board), going home, tilted moves; probing is refused by the engine (no probe hooks: no parameters or expressions on TinyG).\n\n## How tested\n\n- `conformance`: TinyG in POSTS, REFUSED (`tap_plate`, \"tapping\"), EXTENSIONS; the synth stream drops only the tap. Goldens in `golden/nc/tinyg/` (12) and `golden/nc/synth_tinyg.nc`.\n- New `tinyg_post.rs` (11 tests): registry and library; every word letter and G/M code of the posted programs is in TinyG's table; lift, lone `T M6`, `M0`, spindle after; drilling as plain moves with `G4 P1.5`, owed dwell refused; tap refused once; T32 refused, T31 posts; homed machine lifts with G53; unknown or buried lift refused; after-operation M0/M1 counted apart from the tool-change stops, home refused; hostile names; inch output.\n- Cross-post lists extended: `comment_escape`, `control_comp`, `wear_comp`, `post/tests/comp`, `fanuc_post` (non-RTCP), `inverted_post`, `coolant`, `coolant_followups`, `after_op` (home refusal), `machine` (library expectations).\n- **Firmware replay:** every golden and the synth golden replayed through the edge-next firmware's own parser (`tests/host/input_harness.py`) and through its parser + canonical machine + arc generator + planner (`tests/host/corpus_replay.py`, build 450.03, commit d4014951): 13 files, 749 lines, 1626 planner blocks, 0 refused lines, 0 alarms, 0 numeric findings.\n- Gate: all 211 `camcraft-app` test binaries except `lathe_thread_travel` green on the final tree (`--test-threads=6`), `camcraft-post` `comp` 9/9, `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test tinyg_post -- -D warnings` clean. `scripts/gate.sh quick` stops on `lathe_thread_travel.rs:83` (missing field `hand`), the pre-existing break on this branch's base that #712 fixed on main; not touched here.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n**Not yet run on a TinyG board** - the author maintains the edge-next firmware and will dry-run a posted program on a v8 board next (no stock, Z raised, hand on feed hold) and report on #836. The Setup pane's End-units row still appears only for Tormach, although the script reads `EndUnits`. No spindle-up dwell after M3 is written (TinyG suggests `G4 P2` where needed); a post option for it is recorded as a follow-up in the decision file.\n\nChangelog: Synthetos TinyG post processor (3-axis mill) and a generic TinyG 3-axis machine; drilling posts as plain moves with G4 dwells, M0 after each tool change, tapping, G41/G42, probing and go-home refused by name\n\nFixes #836\n",
